## What this lane found

**The headline is a hostile, measured finding against a rule promoted 14 minutes before the freeze.** Delta 17(t)'s δ' = (k+1)·Def 5.1(3) rule is **undefined on two thirds of the frontier**. Def 5.1(3) carries a factor 1/(n − M_s − 1) that is identically 1 for a Keller pair and is never exercised in the source; after descent the anchor n' − M_{s'}' − 1 vanishes exactly when M_{s−1} = n − d_s. Measured: 38 of the 57 descendable screened survivors at n ≤ 100, 12 of the 20 at n = 108, and **three of Moh's printed six** — while every row in Moh's p.207 descent table has a non-degenerate anchor. Theorem (T) can currently only be posed on 19 of 57 rows.

I validated my own descent reconstruction first: it reproduces p.207's (75,50) → (15,10,11; X²) and (64,48) → (16,12,13; X), and the radii rule returns (−1, 1/2) and (−1, 1/4) — the two values `descent-radii-grok46` obtained by numerical Newton–Puiseux. Two independent routes agree, so the rule is right *where it is defined*.

**On the coordinator's framing, two corrections.** Q1's "the uniform kill mechanism b_min > h — can it be turned into an all-degree statement?" is answered NO by the campaign's own data: 25 of the 60 screened survivors satisfy b > h and survive; the kill needs the path-dependent Lemma 5.3 danger flag. The sharper true statement: `lo` = P_j/Q_j identically, so on the n − M_j > d_j stratum the screen is exactly the **divisibility A_j | P_j** — a congruence system, which is why I expect the screened space to be cofinally nonempty and would not stake the proof on it.

**One new avenue proposed, built, and closed negative.** The descent is a functor on characteristic data and the screen consumes only characteristic data, so screens compose along it. I implemented the composite screen and ran it: 0 forced major zeros on the 19 evaluable rows, A₂' = 1 on 8 of them. It is vacuous — which is the strongest evidence yet for the Q4 dichotomy that the proof must be the coefficient computation.

The screen reproduced 658 → 60 → 58 and, run fresh at n = 108, 217 → 21 → 20, all on first run with no repair. Nothing here re-types a promoted claim; H1 is a coverage finding, not a refutation.

**First lane recommended:** `descent-anchor-audit` (4 hours, source + rationals) — the only item on the board that can invalidate a promotion made today, and it determines the domain of theorem (T).
